          "id": "1768431814963",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768431814965_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Goal\nGenerate one email communication suggestion that a manager can send to their team, highlighting suggested learnings.\n\nInputs\n- Data (learning items payload):\n  <data>{{$context.$nodes.GET_LEARNING_ITEMS_FROM_CATALOG.$output}}</data>\n- Sender full name:\n  <sender>{{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}</sender>\n\nValidation and extraction\n- If data.items is missing/not an array/empty, proceed with an empty HTML list and a neutral topic.\n- For each learning item row, extract:\n  - title: learningItemTitle (required, non-empty)\n  - link: learningItemDetailsDeepLink (required, non-empty; use as href)\n  - note: learningItemTypeMeaning (optional; if present, include after the title in parentheses)\n- Build anchors:\n  - <a href=\"learningItemDetailsDeepLink\">learningItemTitle</a>\n  - If note exists, render as “ (note)”\n- Collect learningItemShortDescription from available rows to derive a concise topic (short phrase summarizing common themes). If none, use “recommended learning opportunities”.\n\nEmail body requirements (rich text HTML)\n- Greeting: “Hello Team,”\n- One-line intro referencing the topic, e.g.: “Here are some learning items we can enroll in to build <topic>.”\n- Unordered list of items as:\n  <ul>\n    <li><a href=\"...\">Title</a>(optional note)</li>\n    ...\n  </ul>\n- Valediction and signature on separate lines:\n  Thanks,\n  <sender>\n- Ensure valid HTML; escape special characters in titles/notes, keep URLs intact.\n\nTitle, description, and action text\n- Title: Suggested Learnings\n- Description: One sentence indicating the manager is suggesting learnings to the team based on the topic.\n- Action text: Send\n\nConstraints and style\n- Do not fabricate fields. Skip items missing required title or link.\n- Keep the topic concise and the tone professional yet approachable."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
